cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Belay: durable side effects for nondeterministic agents"
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
abstract: >-
  Replay-based durable execution is correct only under a discipline that no
  framework enforces: every nondeterministic value must be persisted before it
  can influence an external effect. For an LLM agent the decision is the
  control flow, so this is exactly what developers get wrong, and the
  resulting failures are rare, silent, and financial. Belay allocates effect
  identity before the model is consulted, which makes the discipline
  unnecessary. Measured across 960 confirmed SIGKILLs against an external
  ledger: zero contract violations, versus 34-60% for replay and retry
  baselines. Includes an impossibility result showing that escalation is
  necessary rather than conservative when the target service offers neither
  idempotency nor a post-hoc lookup.
authors:
  - name: "Belay contributors"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-14"
keywords:
  - durable execution
  - exactly-once
  - idempotency
  - LLM agents
  - crash recovery
  - distributed systems
